2013-12-05 17:23:57	TheMaverick`	We have a VPN client connection running (!) ... but we are having trouble setting up a second interface for player machines to connect to. Any help?
2013-12-05 17:24:14	!cao	?
2013-12-05 17:24:20	!cao	can you ping the vm?
2013-12-05 17:24:35	TheMaverick`	Fromt eh VPN box, yes.
2013-12-05 17:24:48	!cao	awesome, then you just do NAT
2013-12-05 17:24:54	TheMaverick`	We are trying to setup eth1 for plugging in a switch and connecting players.
2013-12-05 17:25:27	TheMaverick`	Are we not supposed to use the /24 for player machines?
2013-12-05 17:25:36	TheMaverick`	individual*
2013-12-05 17:26:05	!cao	you are not
2013-12-05 17:26:33	TheMaverick`	Oh... so, we are NAT'ing through 10.14.X.1
2013-12-05 17:26:36	fas[pdx]	ooooh...
2013-12-05 17:26:55	TheMaverick`	cao: So, I don't really know how to do this :-S
2013-12-05 17:27:22	-->	ctfpap|eno (noone@ictf2013-5l2.i30.r6na9j.IP) has joined #ictf
2013-12-05 17:27:29	!cao	iptables -t nat -A POSTROUTING -o tun-ictf -j MASQUERADE
2013-12-05 17:27:30	!cao	should work
2013-12-05 17:27:40	!cao	add your local ip as the gateway for that machine
2013-12-05 17:28:54	!cao	so on a player machine, you do: route add 10.14.X.2 gw <the local ip address of your vpn gateway>
2013-12-05 17:29:26	!cao	you might also want to do: sysctl -w net.ipv4.ip_forward=1
2013-12-05 17:29:41	TheMaverick`	cao: We setup ipv4 forwarding
2013-12-05 17:31:05	-->	ricky (ricky@ictf2013-q9m.4ic.75tbv5.IP) has joined #ictf
2013-12-05 17:31:56	someone	we will be using 127.0.0.0/24 for the player machines. This worked like a charm this evening: We all could ping each other with nealy no delay! I just hope nothing breaks tomorrow :/
2013-12-05 17:32:11	!cao	:p
2013-12-05 17:32:34	!cao	i prefer 127.0.0.0/8, moar addresses aint hurt nobody
